# The lines with a girl's name in the middle: {about} is the girl it was about.
# incident: her opening when she heard of something you did (self=yes when it was to her; friend=yes when it was to her friend).
# incident.seen: you and another girl, from a girl who saw it (saw=yes) or heard of it (saw=no); what=kiss|hand|touch|h, none for a sweet word.
# incident.gossip: what she passes on about you; inc is the kind, what the step for a flirt.

# ================= incident =================
@rule incident.helped_defended.self_yes.gentle
on incident
when inc=helped|defended self=yes tone=gentle
- Thank you again for earlier. It really meant a lot.
- Thank you for earlier. It meant so much.
- About earlier... thank you, really.
- I'm still grateful for earlier.

@rule incident.helped_defended.self_yes.energetic
on incident
when inc=helped|defended self=yes tone=energetic
- Hey! Thanks for helping me out, you were awesome!
- Thanks for earlier! You rocked!
- You were amazing earlier! Thanks!
- Earlier? Awesome! Thanks!

@rule incident.helped_defended.self_yes.cool
on incident
when inc=helped|defended self=yes tone=cool
- About earlier. ...Thanks.
- Earlier. ...Thank you.
- About earlier. Thanks.
- ...Thanks for earlier.

@rule incident.helped_defended.self_yes.teasing
on incident
when inc=helped|defended self=yes tone=teasing
- You were pretty cool earlier. Don't let it go to your head.
- Pretty cool earlier. Don't gloat.
- You did well earlier. Stay humble.
- Earlier? Not bad. Don't brag.

@rule incident.helped_defended.self_no.gentle
on incident
when inc=helped|defended self=no tone=gentle
- {about} told me you helped her. That was really kind of you.
- {about} said you helped her. So kind.
- I heard you helped {about}... that's sweet.
- {about} told me what you did. Thank you.

